erlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n</span> Notes</a></div>\n  <div class=\"wprm-layout-column-container wprm-column-gap-40 wprm-column-rows-recipe-900 meadow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10826-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-10826-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"10826\" data-servings=\"8\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Dry Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">all-purpose flour</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for the base of your dough</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"2\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">sugar</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">to add a hint of sweetness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"3\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">balances the flavors</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"4\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">baking powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for that perfect puffiness</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Wet Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"6\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">unsalted butter</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">softened for richness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"7\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">3/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">warm water</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">or milk for a richer flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"8\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Oil for frying</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">necessary for that crispy exterior</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-10826-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10826\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Deep Skillet or Pot&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For frying the dough</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Rolling Pin&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For rolling out the dough</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Paper towels&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For draining excess oil</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-10826-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-10826-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"10826\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation Steps</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a bowl, whisk together flour, sugar, salt, and baking powder until well combined.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Cut in softened butter until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs. It should feel a bit like sand!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Gradually add warm water or milk and stir until a soft dough forms. Don’t be shy; get in there!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Knead the dough on a floured surface for 2–3 minutes until it’s smooth and elastic. You got this!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Cover the dough and let it rest for 10 minutes. This is the dough’s time to relax!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Divide the dough into equal portions and roll each into a thin round. Make them as big or small as you like!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Heat oil in a deep skillet or pot to 350°F (175°C). Be careful; it’s hot in there!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Fry each dough round until puffed and golden, about 1–2 minutes per side. Flip them with love!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-10826-step-0-8\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Drain on paper towels and serve warm. Enjoy your delicious fried dough!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-10826-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrition Facts</th>\n<th>Per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>7g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s what you&#8217;ll need to make your delicious <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fried_dough\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">fried dough</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Fried-Dough-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for fried dough arranged on a kitchen table, including flour, sugar, salt, baking powder, butter, warm water, and oil.\" class=\"wp-image-10824\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Fried-Dough-Preparation.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Fried-Dough-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 cups all-purpose flour</strong> – for the base of your dough</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons sugar</strong> – to add a hint of sweetness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon salt</strong> – balances the flavors</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon baking powder</strong> – for that perfect puffiness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons unsalted butter</strong> – softened for richness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>3/4 cup warm water</strong> – or milk for a richer flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Oil for frying</strong> – necessary for that crispy exterior</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-fried-dough\"><strong>How to Make Fried Dough</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready for a delightful treat! This fried dough recipe takes about 10 minutes to prepare, 5 minutes to cook, and an extra 10 minutes for resting. Let’s dive in!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Fried-Dough-Preparation-Steps.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making fried dough, showcasing ingredients and preparation techniques.\" class=\"wp-image-10825\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Fried-Dough-Preparation-Steps.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Fried-Dough-Preparation-Steps-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Whisk Dry Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, whisk together flour, sugar, salt, and baking powder until well combined.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Cut in Butter</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cut in softened butter until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs. It should feel a bit like sand!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add Liquid</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gradually add warm water or milk and stir until a soft dough forms. Don’t be shy; get in there!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Knead the Dough</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Knead the dough on a floured surface for 2–3 minutes until it’s smooth and elastic. You got this!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Let it Rest</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cover the dough and let it rest for 10 minutes. This is the dough’s time to relax!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Divide and Roll</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Divide the dough into equal portions and roll each into a thin round. Make them as big or small as you like!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Heat the Oil</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat oil in a deep skillet or pot to 350°F (175°C). Be careful; it’s hot in there!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Fry the Dough</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fry each dough round until puffed and golden, about 1–2 minutes per side. Flip them with love!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Drain and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Drain on paper towels and serve warm. Enjoy your delicious fried dough!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Dessert / snacks</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>10 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm and crispy</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-fried-dough\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Fried Dough</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Let the dough rest for at least 30 minutes for a lighter texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a thermometer to ensure your oil is at the right temperature (around 350°F).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Roll the dough out evenly for consistent cooking and a perfect shape.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with different toppings like cinnamon sugar or powdered sugar for variety.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve immediately for the best taste and texture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-fried-dough\"><strong>How to Serve this fried dough</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Dust with powdered sugar for a sweet treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a side of warm chocolate sauce for dipping.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with fresh fruit and whipped cream for a delightful dessert.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle with honey or maple syrup for a classic touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a scoop of vanilla ice cream for an indulgent dessert.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a sprinkle of cinnamon sugar for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a fruit compote for a fruity twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try with a savory dip like garlic butter for a unique flavor experience.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your fried dough later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Let fried dough cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container or wrap tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool fried dough completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap each piece in plastic wrap, then place in a freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For best results, reheat in an oven at 350°F (175°C) for 10-15 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use an air fryer for 5-7 minutes for extra crispiness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Microwave for a quick option, but it may lose some crispiness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is fried dough called?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Fried dough is often referred to by various names depending on the region. In some places, it’s called &#8216;elephant ears,&#8217; &#8216;beaver tails,&#8217; or &#8216;fried bread.&#8217; Each name may refer to a slightly different style or preparation, but they all share the deliciousness of being fried dough!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What is fried dough made of?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Fried dough is typically made from a simple mixture of flour, water, yeast, and a bit of sugar and salt. Some recipes may include milk or baking powder for added flavor and texture. The dough is rolled out and then deep-fried until golden brown, resulting in a crispy exterior and soft interior!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Is fried dough a New England thing?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While fried dough is popular in New England, especially at fairs and carnivals, it is enjoyed in many cultures around the world. Each region has its own twist on the recipe, making it a beloved treat in various forms globally!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Is fried dough the same as funnel cake?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Fried dough and funnel cake are similar but not the same. Funnel cake is made by pouring a thin batter through a funnel into hot oil, creating a lacy pattern, while fried dough is typically a thicker dough that is rolled out and fried. Both are delicious, but they offer different textures and experiences!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have this easy fried dough recipe in your hands, it’s time to gather your loved ones and enjoy the delightful crunch and warmth of homemade goodness! Whether you sprinkle them with sugar or dip them in your favorite sauce, these golden treats are sure to bring smiles and nostalgia. Happy frying!</p>\n",
